         State Election - Tuesday, November 3, 2026 The Commonwealth of Massachusetts will hold a State Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026. This ballot will feature candidates for the following state-wide offices: U.S. Senator U.S. Representative Governor Lieutenant Governor Attorney General Secretary of State Treasurer Auditor Governor’s Councilor State Senator State Representative District Attorney Register of Probate Regional School Committee You can find a sample ballot  here . How & Where Do I Vote? Any registered voter may vote in one of four ways: In Person on Election Day:  You can vote in person at your polling place on Tuesday, November 3, 2026 between the hours of 7 AM and 8 PM. Voters at precinct 1 and precinct 2 vote at Tyngsborough Middle School (50 Norris Road) and voters in precinct 3 and precinct 4 vote at Tyngsborough Elementary School (205 Westford Road). Find out which precinct you belong to  here . By Mail:  Any registered voter may request to vote by mail. If you are interested in voting by mail, you can apply to vote by mail  here . Applications to vote by mail must be received by Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 5:00 PM. Absentee Ballot : If you are unable to vote in person on election day because you will be traveling or otherwise unavailable, you can apply to vote absentee. You can learn more about absentee voting, download an application, and learn more about deadlines by clicking  here . Early Voting : The Town Clerk's Office will provide early voting as required by state law. All early voting will take place at Town Hall (25 Bryant Lane). The early voting schedule is below: Registered voters do not need to apply to early vote or schedule an appointment. Any registered voter may show up to Town Hall during the times listed below and cast their ballot in person.  Saturday, October 17, 2026  : 9 AM to 3 PM Monday, October 19, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM Tuesday, October 20, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM Wednesday, October 21 , 2026  : 8:30 AM to 7:00 PM Thursday, October 22, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 4:00 PM Saturday, October 24, 2026  : 9 AM to 3 PM Monday, October 26, 2026   : 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM Tuesday, October 27, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 4:30 PM Wednesday, October 28, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 7:00 PM Thursday, October 29, 2026  : 8:30 AM to 4:00 PM How do I register to vote? You can find out whether you're registered  to vote by visiting  this link  here . If you are not registered to vote, you can register to vote in person or  online  by  October 24,  2026 .  To register in person, simply visit the Office of the Town Clerk at 25 Bryant Lane anytime during normal business hours. Please note the clerk's office will be open on Saturday, October 24, 2026 until 5:00 PM for in-person voter registration. Special Town Election - Saturday, December 5, 2026 The Town of Tyngsborough will convene a Special Town Election on Saturday, December 5, 2026 to consider whether or not to authorize a debt exclusion to fund the acquisition of 100 Potash Hill Road and the design of a future public safety building at the site. This election was set by the Select Board at their meeting on September 21, 2026. Voter Registration Deadline:  Tuesday, November 24, 2026 at 5:00 PM - You can check your registration status and register to vote  here . You may also contact the Town Clerk's Office by calling 978-649-2300 x129. Request to Vote by Mail : You can request to vote by mail for this election through 5:00 PM on Tuesday, November 24, 2026. Note that any resident who already requested a mail-in ballot for all elections in 2026 will automatically receive a mail-in ballot for this election. You can request a mail-in ballot  here . Absentee Voting:  If you are unable to vote in person on election day because you will be traveling or otherwise unavailable, you can apply to vote absentee. You can learn more about absentee voting, download an application, and learn more about deadlines by clicking  here . 
     

 
